## Lore

Not every spacer is content making a living by honest, or semi-honest, trade.
Some turn to smuggling; some become full-time marauders. Space pirates are hated
and feared by the spacers and travellers who see them as parasites, thieves and
murderers.

The life has been romanticized by books and films. In reality it is harsh,
brutal and often short. Most pirates fly light ships that can damage and take a
small merchantman and are helpless against a real warship or even a
well-defended freighter. They are unwelcome at most spaceports, and at the ones
that will have them there is always the risk of running into a galactic tracer,
or a victim''s friend or relative looking for payback.

## Not all of them chose it

A few joined because they had no choice, and those often keep a rough code that
stops them murdering or molesting innocent people. Plenty of ex-pirates have
switched sides and become law-enforcers, freedom fighters or ordinary spacers.

The typical pirate is none of those. He is a cutthroat who will do whatever it
takes to get what he wants, and who will turn on his own crew if it pays.

## GM Notes

Available as a player character, and as an NPC villain - the book says both.

**The money line has two halves.** A pirate starts with 2D6x1000 credits *and*
1D6x1000 credits'' worth of goods for trade or sale. Only the coin is on the
sheet; roll the goods at the table and decide what they are.

The GM may let a pirate own **a small spaceship** with room for two to eight
passengers and a little cargo. The catalog has no shape for a vessel.

Up to 1D4 cybernetic implants, more purchasable, and the book adds that borgs
and headhunters are always welcome in a pirate''s crew. None of that is on the
sheet.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'space-pirate');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'space-pirate';

